 :context
 "Ongoing careful, smaller-batch rollout (capable model + mandatory verification per
  agent) after a prior 18-agent haiku batch had a 61% defect rate. 60+ consecutive
  agents on this stricter protocol succeeded before this one. Built from
  cloud-itonami-isic-0125 (growing of other tree and bush fruits and nuts) as the
  module-structure template, with clojure -M:test independently re-run from fresh
  clones before and after push. Registry entry independently re-verified fresh
  before any work began: {:id \"0126\" :name \"Growing of oleaginous fruits\" ...}
  genuinely matches (no ID/name mismatch, a known failure mode in this fleet). No
  prior repository existed at cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0126 or the stale
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0126 placeholder (404 confirmed)."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct field-equipment operation (grower's exclusive authority)"
  "finalizing a spray-application decision (agronomist/grower authority)"
  "harvest-timing / replanting economic decisions (remain human authority)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0126 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0125 module-for-module,
  namespace oleaginousops.*):
  - Governor (OleaginousOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks
    (plantation-not-registered, no-execution, field-equipment-or-spray-blocked,
    op-not-allowed, plantation-count-invalid) + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate
    crop-health concern, cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (seedling/fertilizer/equipment),
    fruit classes (oil-palm/coconut = palm; olive = drupe; candlenut = nut)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    plantation-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-plantation lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0125's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-plantation-record, schedule-field-operation,
    flag-crop-health-concern (e.g. bud rot/Ganoderma boninense/drought-stress,
    always escalates), order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 31 tests / 99 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green -- same shape as 0125's own 31-test structure (4 fruit classes vs 0125's
    7 accounts for the 105 -> 99 assertion-count difference; 15 governor-test cases
    with bud-rot/Ganoderma and drought-stress escalation cases swapped in for
    0125's spotted-wing-drosophila/walnut-blight ones)
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/business-model/operator-guide describe the real API"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Oleaginous-fruit-growing (0126) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "Scope boundaries (field-equipment operation, spray-application finalization)
    hardcoded in governor checks, not just asserted in prose"
   "Crop-health escalation (flag-crop-health-concern always human, e.g. bud
    rot/Ganoderma boninense/drought-stress) is a core design invariant"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0125's own stub status"]}

